From: bluelightsaber <26096600+bluelightsaber@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] minigbm: drop DRM master after opening the node

With simpledrm (card node only) the allocator opened card0 first and kept
DRM master, so drm_hwcomposer fell back to a fake 1024x768 display.
---
diff --git a/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc b/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc
index 706dee9..dee8210 100644
--- a/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc
+++ b/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc
@@ -109,6 +109,12 @@ static struct driver *init_try_node(int idx, char const *str)
 	if (fd < 0)
 		return NULL;
 
+	/*
+	 * With card nodes (simpledrm has no render node) the first opener becomes DRM master; the allocator
+	 * only needs dumb buffers, so give master up for the composer (drm_hwcomposer needs it for KMS).
+	 */
+	drmDropMaster(fd);
+
 	drv = drv_create(fd, NULL);
 	if (!drv)
 		close(fd);
